1. Golden-vector test — do this first. The spec wasn't executable (BytesAt is a def, so instance search wouldn't unfold it). I fixed that: one Decidable instance plus rebracketing two quantifiers in ShaPadded, and now clauses decide. The Demo section builds a synthetic MSO and runs five checks — two positive, three negative — which is what confirmed the +32/+35 device-key offsets aren't aliased. The real win is next: dump a ConcreteGiven from Rust, emit it as a Witness, decide each clause. That validates all seven clauses against the implementation at once, and transcription drift is the likeliest way a spec like this goes wrong. Right now the only cross-checks are cborLen_keys and my synthetic layout.

2. Discharge IssuerFormat per-schema. Write the mDL MSO encoder in Lean and prove IssuerFormat (encode m) _ m. Turns five assumptions into one theorem plus "the issuer uses this encoder." The hard obligation is that no field value can contain a key literal, which for text and byte strings is a length argument. This is the thing you said you ultimately want, and it's real work.

3. Four circuit changes, each deleting a residual-trust item — likely cheaper than proving around them. Assert the namespace (K_NAMESPACE_CHECK_CBOR already exists, unused). Compare the docType CBOR string's declared length, turning prefix into equality. Assert e < p, dpkX < p, dpkY < p — three bv.lt calls, and AgreesModP disappears. Constrain the attribute digest offset to the valueDigests map extent; doesn't remove the SHA-256 dependence but shrinks the target set enormously.

4. Prove #E(F_p256) = n. Discharges h_pk_order/h_G_order/h_R_order in ecdsa_circuit_soundness — currently the circuit asserts only is_on_curve. Standard route is n prime (Pratt.lean is already there) plus n·G = O plus Hasse's bound; check whether Mathlib has Hasse before committing.

5. Replace the long ∧-chains with structures. AttrOk is an 11-way right-nested conjunction and obtain patterns against it are positional and brittle — I miscounted twice writing the transfer proofs, and both failures surfaced as confusing elimination errors rather than "wrong field." Named fields would make the eventual artifact-to-spec bridge much more maintainable.

6. WellFormed is a dangling side condition. ValidPresentation is only a faithful reading of the circuit under it. Either fold it in or make the fixed-width truncation explicit in the clauses.